From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] plugin: hash a device node by its device number, not its
 times

A plugin's external dependency on device nodes, such as va's on
/dev/dri/renderD* or v4l2codecs' on /dev/video*, is hashed by the
nodes' size, mtime and ctime. The kernel updates a node's times as the
device is used, so any program that opens the GPU makes the cached
plugin stale and the next process to start rescans it and rewrites the
whole registry: on an RK3528, half a second of every browser start.
A node names the same device while its device number is the same, so
hash that.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
---
--- a/gst/gstplugin.c
+++ b/gst/gstplugin.c
@@ -1673,6 +1673,13 @@
 #endif
     return (guint) - 1;
 
+#ifndef G_OS_WIN32
+  /* a device node's times change as it is used; the device is the same while
+   * its number is */
+  if (S_ISCHR (s->st_mode) || S_ISBLK (s->st_mode))
+    return (guint) s->st_rdev;
+#endif
+
   /* completely random formula */
   return ((s->st_size << 3) + (s->st_mtime << 5)) ^ s->st_ctime;
 }
